On 22.01.2013 16:45, G-Mon wrote:
> 
> Anyway, I believe I was originally talking about displacement vs. MC3; 
> my opinion on that is that displacement both more and less dangerous 
> that MC3, in different ways: displacement means you get hit less often, 
> but anything that has to bypass your MC (e.g. a wraith's level drain 
> attack) has an easier time working if it does hit; as for hard-hitters, 
> being *less* likely to hit you doesn't mean much if the RNG's 
> sufficiently moody. In a nutshell, displacement's good if you get it, 
> but don't rely solely on it.

Sure, but you can't have the cake and eat it too; you can't get both
from cloaks. (You'd need body armor which doesn't fit for the monks
we're talking about in this thread.) MC3 is most useful in the early
game, IMO; the secondary effects of lycanthropy are bad. Though early
displacement is also very nice, and it's still nice to have it later!
But MC3 quickly gets less important; two main threats are cockatrices
(though they appear about at the same time when lizards start to appear
in the game), and the vampires you mention. Vampires in morgues are no
big problem, since there's always some undead popcorn critters as well
that will immediately restore your lost level if you kill it (usually
with a single strike). And the E-word will give you the necessary time
between the blows. Only a bit care is necessary to not get cocky.

